{
  "id": "m5l1",
  "title": {
    "es": "Argumentos flexibles",
    "en": "Flexible arguments"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Valores por defecto"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Un parámetro puede tener un **valor por defecto** que se usa si no se pasa ese argumento. Los parámetros con defecto van **después** de los obligatorios."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "def saluda(nombre, saludo=\"Hola\"):",
          "    return f\"{saludo}, {nombre}\"",
          "",
          "print(saluda(\"Ana\"))",
          "print(saluda(\"Ana\", \"Buenas\"))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "Hola, Ana",
          "Buenas, Ana"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "*args y **kwargs"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`*args` recoge un número variable de argumentos posicionales en una **tupla**; `**kwargs` recoge los argumentos con nombre en un **diccionario**."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "def suma(*numeros):",
          "    total = 0",
          "    for n in numeros:",
          "        total += n",
          "    return total",
          "",
          "print(suma(1, 2, 3, 4))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "10"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Una función también puede **devolver varios valores** a la vez (como tupla) y desempaquetarlos."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "def divide(a, b):",
          "    return a // b, a % b",
          "",
          "cociente, resto = divide(17, 5)",
          "print(cociente, resto)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "3 2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Evita listas/diccionarios como valor por defecto (`def f(x=[])`): se **comparten** entre llamadas y causan errores sutiles."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Default values"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "A parameter can have a **default value** used when that argument isn't passed. Parameters with defaults go **after** the required ones."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "def saluda(nombre, saludo=\"Hola\"):",
          "    return f\"{saludo}, {nombre}\"",
          "",
          "print(saluda(\"Ana\"))",
          "print(saluda(\"Ana\", \"Buenas\"))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "Hola, Ana",
          "Buenas, Ana"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "*args and **kwargs"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`*args` collects a variable number of positional arguments into a **tuple**; `**kwargs` collects named arguments into a **dict**."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "def suma(*numeros):",
          "    total = 0",
          "    for n in numeros:",
          "        total += n",
          "    return total",
          "",
          "print(suma(1, 2, 3, 4))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "10"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "A function can also **return several values** at once (as a tuple) and unpack them."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "def divide(a, b):",
          "    return a // b, a % b",
          "",
          "cociente, resto = divide(17, 5)",
          "print(cociente, resto)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "3 2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Avoid lists/dicts as default values (`def f(x=[])`): they are **shared** across calls and cause subtle bugs."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m5l1e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `suma_todos(*numeros)` que devuelva la suma de **todos** los argumentos que reciba (0 si no recibe ninguno).",
        "en": "Define `suma_todos(*numeros)` returning the sum of **all** arguments it receives (0 if none)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def suma_todos(*numeros):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def suma_todos(*numeros):",
        "    return sum(numeros)"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "*numeros es una tupla con todos los argumentos.",
          "sum(numeros) los suma."
        ],
        "en": [
          "*numeros is a tuple with all arguments.",
          "sum(numeros) adds them."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "suma_todos",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                1,
                2,
                3
              ],
              "expected": 6
            },
            {
              "args": [
                10
              ],
              "expected": 10
            },
            {
              "args": [],
              "expected": 0
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m5l1e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `repite(texto, veces=2)` que devuelva el texto repetido `veces` veces (por defecto 2).",
        "en": "Define `repite(texto, veces=2)` returning the text repeated `veces` times (default 2)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def repite(texto, veces=2):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def repite(texto, veces=2):",
        "    return texto * veces"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Una cadena por un número se repite: 'ab'*3 == 'ababab'."
        ],
        "en": [
          "A string times a number repeats it: 'ab'*3 == 'ababab'."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "repite",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                "ab"
              ],
              "expected": "abab"
            },
            {
              "args": [
                "ab",
                3
              ],
              "expected": "ababab"
            },
            {
              "args": [
                "hi"
              ],
              "expected": "hihi"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}